==Battleground==
*1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*20 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 1.33~2 seconds<sup>40f~60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Ancient Magamojoe]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 2.67~3.33 seconds<sup>80f~100f</sup>.
**1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**2 [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Berserkory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The startoff of this stage is relatively simple, although Dagshund's high health may catch you off guard. [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] is recommended here.

When you hit the base, you fight a combination of Magamojoe and Berserkory. Unfortunately for this stage, both of these enemies are fodder for [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. Literally spam [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], UL Legends, and maybe [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2/NX]] alongside Courier and you win.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Luna can Freeze both Ancient Magamojoe and Berserkory, while also blocking its waves. Magamojoe's Surge Attacks can be a little troublesome but she should generally be able to handle it.

==Trivia==
*Hole Lotta Somethin's Japanese name, Shiranke Dō (シランケ洞, "I-Don't-Know Cave"), is a pun on ''shiran kedo'' (知らんけど), a [[wikipedia:Kansai dialect|Kansai dialect]] term that can roughly be translated as "I don't know, ''but...''" The joke is that instead of ど ''do'', the stage name is spelled with the kanji 洞 ''dō'', meaning "cave".

